      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Two major railroads—Missouri Pacific and Atchison, Topeka & Santa Fe—ran through Elk City, turning it into a regional hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://legendsofkansas.com/elk-city-kansas/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic 1st Christian Church, built in 1900, was lost to fire in May 2015, marking a significant loss for the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://legendsofkansas.com/elk-city-kansas/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Elk City feels like a near ghost town today, with several abandoned buildings echoing its past prosperity.",
